 "subs": [
  {
   "text": "71 files",
   "start": 17.417,
   "duration": 13.81,
   "x": -560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "1.42 GB build",
   "start": 17.867,
   "duration": 13.36,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "one .rbpack = 95%",
   "start": 18.317,
   "duration": 12.91,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "1 person, Austria",
   "start": 18.767,
   "duration": 12.46,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Every demo I've taken apart on this channel was made\nin Unity, by people who write code. This one wasn't.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 6.21
  },
  {
   "text": "It was made in a tool sold on the promise that you never have\nto program. There's a C# compiler inside the build anyway.",
   "start": 6.46,
   "duration": 6.707
  },
  {
   "text": "Veiled Shadows is a month in a rural mountain town. You build\nbonds during the day, and at night you go into another world.",
   "start": 17.017,
   "duration": 7.229
  },
  {
   "text": "Everyone who has played it reaches for the same word:\nPersona. One reviewer counted the nods to Persona 4.",
   "start": 24.496,
   "duration": 6.681
  },
  {
   "text": "The battle menu is drawn as a handheld console,\nand your abilities are cartridges you slot into it.",
   "start": 31.427,
   "duration": 5.688
  },
  {
   "text": "The demo went up five days ago. Six reviews, all positive. That's\nnot a reception, so what I can actually read here is the build.",
   "start": 37.365,
   "duration": 7.961
  },
  {
   "text": "Steam publishes the file list for every\ndemo. This one has seventy one entries.",
   "start": 45.576,
   "duration": 5.087
  },
  {
   "text": "The engine is RPG Developer Bakin, from a Japanese studio called SmileBoom.\nSeventy dollars on Steam, and it's sold as programming-free RPG creation.",
   "start": 50.913,
   "duration": 10.286
  },
  {
   "text": "The game's own executable is five hundred\nand sixty two kilobytes. It's a launcher.",
   "start": 61.449,
   "duration": 5.27
  },
  {
   "text": "What actually runs the game is bakinplayer.exe,\nand the engine DLL sitting next to it.",
   "start": 66.969,
   "duration": 6.524
  },
  {
   "text": "Then there's one file\nthat is the entire game.",
   "start": 73.743,
   "duration": 2.814
  },
  {
   "text": "data.rbpack. One point three five gigabytes.\nNinety five percent of the download.",
   "start": 76.807,
   "duration": 5.923
  },
  {
   "text": "Every map, every model, every portrait and every\nvoice line this person made is inside that one file.",
   "start": 82.98,
   "duration": 6.524
  },
  {
   "text": "The other seventy entries are the\nengine, shipped exactly as it arrived.",
   "start": 89.754,
   "duration": 4.434
  },
  {
   "text": "Which is the interesting part, because of what\na no-code tool puts in your game without asking.",
   "start": 94.438,
   "duration": 5.427
  },
  {
   "text": "First. Microsoft.CodeAnalysis, two DLLs, ten point\nseven megabytes. That's Roslyn. That is a C# compiler.",
   "start": 100.115,
   "duration": 8.979
  },
  {
   "text": "Bakin does offer an optional C# scripting feature, and this is what pays for it. Every\ngame made in the tool carries a compiler, whether its author wrote a line of C# or not.",
   "start": 109.344,
   "duration": 10.703
  },
  {
   "text": "Second. WebView2, and an Edge browser control.\nThere is a web browser inside this turn-based RPG.",
   "start": 120.297,
   "duration": 7.882
  },
  {
   "text": "I could not work out what it's for from a file list. If you've\nbuilt something in Bakin, the comments are right there.",
   "start": 128.429,
   "duration": 6.472
  },
  {
   "text": "Third, and this is the one\nworth taking away. VRM Loader.",
   "start": 135.151,
   "duration": 4.539
  },
  {
   "text": "VRM is the avatar format VRoid Studio\nexports. The format VTubers use.",
   "start": 139.94,
   "duration": 5.74
  },
  {
   "text": "So a solo developer can pull a 3D character out of an\navatar maker instead of modelling one from scratch.",
   "start": 145.93,
   "duration": 6.054
  },
  {
   "text": "The shaders ship as plain text, uncompiled. Seven include files,\nthirty eight kilobytes between them. One is six bytes long.",
   "start": 152.234,
   "duration": 7.882
  },
  {
   "text": "They get compiled on your machine when you play. That's what the\nseventeen megabyte DirectX shader compiler next to them is for.",
   "start": 160.366,
   "duration": 7.308
  },
  {
   "text": "And there's a log file in there. bakinplayer_log.txt,\nfrom the developer's own session, shipped to players.",
   "start": 167.924,
   "duration": 7.229
  },
  {
   "text": "It's fourteen kilobytes. Two episodes ago the same mistake was seven hundred\nand seventy megabytes of debug symbols. Four orders of magnitude apart.",
   "start": 175.403,
   "duration": 8.953
  },
  {
   "text": "There are four readme files too, in English, Japanese and both kinds of Chinese, on a store page that\nlists English only. Those are the engine's own readmes, which tells you the folder went out untouched.",
   "start": 184.606,
   "duration": 12.192
  },
  {
   "text": "Now the six reviews. You can't count\nsix of anything, but you can read them.",
   "start": 197.048,
   "duration": 4.591
  },
  {
   "text": "One of them tells me the developer is one person in Austria.\nThat's the team size, from a player, not a press kit.",
   "start": 201.889,
   "duration": 6.628
  },
  {
   "text": "Two of them mention the voice acting, unprompted. And one\nhad seven hours on a demo that covers a few in-game days.",
   "start": 208.767,
   "duration": 6.863
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 215.88,
   "duration": 2.344
  },
  {
   "text": "Bakin, seventy dollars, one person. One point three five gigabytes of\ntheir content against sixty seven megabytes of engine they didn't write.",
   "start": 218.474,
   "duration": 8.117
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip, and worth\nit for the art alone.",
   "start": 226.841,
   "duration": 2.814
  },
  {
   "text": "If somebody has told you no-code means a low ceiling, this\nbuild ships a C# compiler. The ceiling is wherever you stop.",
   "start": 229.905,
   "duration": 8.065
  },
  {
   "text": "And before you publish, open your engine folder. That's my read from the outside, though. If you made this and I got\nsomething wrong, say so and I'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 238.22,
   "duration": 13.316
  }
 ],
